            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 10,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "If we're going to change here, we need to get more specific.  \"Name1/Name2\" was something done when TMP421 was the most complicated thing supported.\n\nIF we're going more specific, they would be direct names of the inputs\n\n```\n{\n   Type: NCT7802,\n   Voltage1Name: \"My volts\",\n   Voltage2Name: \"My second volts\",\n   Temp1Name: \"My temp sensor\",\n}\n```\n\nThat way we're not assigning arbitrary indexes, and when someone looks at a schematic, they can write this file successfully.  Put another way, there's no way to know that \"ExtraNames\" index 0 is a fan.\n\nFWIW, i think some of the issue here is that NCT7802 shouldn't have been put in hwmontempsensor, as it includes more than just temp sensors.  I'm happy to see things extended, but lets do them in a way that we don't have ambiguity in the config format.\n\nAlternatively, we we move this chip to be in PSUSensor instead of Hwmontempsensor, I suspect we can use the format as-is."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 10,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "/s/we we/if we/g"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 10,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "> Alternatively, we we move this chip to be in PSUSensor instead of Hwmontempsensor\n\nI'm not super excited about moving anything to PSUSensor schema. It's a legacy schema and has lots of antipatterns.\n\n```\n{\n   Type: NCT7802,\n   Voltage1Name: \"My volts\",\n   Voltage2Name: \"My second volts\",\n   Temp1Name: \"My temp sensor\",\n}\n```\n\nYour example would result in roughly one schema per type of chip to be supported.\n\nThat's the reverse of what's historically been done in EM, where multiple chips are supported by one schema. I'm not really against it but that's a schema discussion which is probably best done in EM.\n\nLet's keep schema discussion contained to the EM repo."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 18,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "I was part of that discussion, and don't really understand why this is needed.  Regardless, commit messages should be able to justify support in isolation, links should be used for more details."
                },
